vmhal3d (JHRobotics/vmhal9x 8bc480e) colour transfers between GL and a DirectDraw surface
(MesaBufferUploadColor / MesaBufferDownloadColor) assumed rows of exactly width x bytes per
pixel. Flip-chain surfaces have the screen's pitch, which the NV50 driver pads to a 256-byte
multiple (800x600x16 = 1792 bytes, not 1600): every frame was copied with a 96-pixel shear
per row (horizontal streaks). Now the target's real pitch is kept (ctx->front_pitch, from the
surface record) and passed as GL_(UN)PACK_ROW_LENGTH when it differs. Dungeon Keeper 2 at
800x600, found 2026-10-31. Apply after vmhal3d-ddfifo.patch and vmhal3d-flatshade.patch.

--- a/mesa3d.h
+++ b/mesa3d.h
@@ -296,6 +296,7 @@
 	DWORD thread_id;
 	GLint front_bpp;
 	GLint depth_bpp;
+	DWORD front_pitch; /* bytes per row of the target surface in VRAM, 0 = packed */
 	//DDRAWI_DDRAWSURFACE_LCL flips[MESA3D_MAX_FLIPS];
 	//int flips_cnt;
 	DWORD backbuffer;
